// M5-A3P-1006. Ch19 I02 "The vigil" (P walk → C, 4 min). act3_ch19.md §2 I02; ADR 0017; ADR 0020 (g).
// RULE 1: THE PROLOGUE'S FRAME, SHOT FOR SHOT (prologue_dead_city: P01 fixed wide, P02 the two-shot on the rise): the
// broken plaza at dusk, all seven APART, no fire; Kerrid standing; Pell with his back to the sea; Ysolde with her book
// shut; Asha on the steps. Each companion goes to their Prologue place without being told (the walk is the player's;
// one look or gesture each, no words). Rhen sits by Asha and trims his lantern's wick (his oil lantern, NOT Kell's
// wick): the only flame. THE LINE PLAYS VERBATIM; it is the human's (ADR 0020 (g)): never reword it, add nothing.
// It has its own id here so the Prologue's line and this one can be cued apart; the text must stay identical to
// prologue_dead_city_001. T-07 / M4-A2P-111: the Prologue's "glimmer rises around him" is NOT repeated (nothing rises
// before H09). RULE 2: nothing names Imra, Dace and Kerrid together.
title: ch19_the_vigil
location: ch19/iskarra
---
@anim kerrid vigil_stand
@anim pell turn_back sea
@anim ysolde vigil_book_shut
@anim asha sit plaza_steps
@wait 2.0
@letterbox on
@camera P01
@light LanternLight off
@wait 3.5
@mark rhen by_asha walk
@camera P02 blend=7.0 ease=in_out_sine
@anim rhen look_at asha
@wait 1.0
@anim rhen trim_wicks
@light LanternLight on 1.4
@wait 0.6
Narrator(rhen) [tender]: Everyone I'm going to tell you about is still here tonight. Remember that, later. #line:ch19_vigil_001 #vo #tn:"Must stay word for word the same as prologue_dead_city_001, in every language: the same line, heard again."
@wait 4.0
@camera P01
@wait 6.0
<<set $ch19_vigil = true>>
@fade out 2.5
@letterbox off
===
